#text(fill: blue, weight: "bold")[[Standard vs. Product]] Problem is that standard produced near the center of the manufacturing specificiations *may not covered the acutual variations of products* produced at the extremes of the manufacturing specifications. It means that gauge stabilty *may not be covered all potential situations* if gauge capability was measured using only *standard*.

#text(fill: blue, weight: "bold")[[Unconstant variance]] Secondly, *the variance may not measured exactly* if the measurement of gauge capability is performed using the limited products or only standards. In other words, the variance may be unconstant. R chart generally recommands to detect nonconstant but it have some limitations. 

#text(fill: blue, weight: "bold")[[Need new part]] Third, a new part provides more chances for knowing the sources of variation to occur in the measurement process than repeat measurement of *same part*.

